    rdfs:comment "COMPLETED (W2 SP0, plan T1-T11) — the deepest floor basicttl/foundation/, the four-pillar bedrock the whole ontology stands on (Directive 18 algebra<-set-theory + space constructs; Directive 19 the functionality/Curry-F fourth pillar; Directive 20 MAXIMAL depth, all teeth-proved). Reproducible on disk via `bash basicttl/foundation/checks/run-foundation-checks.sh` (exit 0, GREEN): the merged SP0+SP1+SP2+SP3 graph conforms to foundation.shapes.ttl (45 sh:NodeShape teeth) AND to the prior-floor laws re-run over the SP0-augmented merge (primitives.shapes.ttl dual-grounding tooth, crs.shapes.ttl, aob.shapes.ttl full re-validation), with 42 foundation + 21 SP1 + 13 SP2 + 10 SP3 EXPECT-TRUE ASKs all true and the depth gate green (every owl:Class >=200-char rdfs:comment, 10 files); SP1/SP2/SP3 stay untouched and green standalone and over the merge. Real counts, freshly recounted on disk (rdflib/grep, Fix-B; each asserted EQUAL to its recomputed disk value against BOTH this DAG node and basicttl/foundation/README.md by the runner count self-check, step 5d -- any drift in either surface goes RED): 80 fnd owl:Class, 129 fnd owl:ObjectProperty, 23 fnd owl:DatatypeProperty, 608 distinct fnd subjects each honesty-tagged, merged SP0+SP1+SP2+SP3 = 15541 triples (SP0-only = 3909 triples), 45 SHACL teeth, 42 ASKs, 19 named fnd:probe* identifiers. Fix-A completeness hardening (A1 two-operation-line associativity/commutativity + A2 quasigroup totality): the Semiring->Ring->Field line reifies its two operations via fnd:ringStructure (DISTINCT from the spine fnd:opStructure the T4 assoc/comm teeth walk), so additive associativity, additive commutativity and multiplicative associativity were NEVER teeth-checked over the ring operations - fnd:RingAddAssocShape/fnd:RingAddCommShape/fnd:RingMultAssocShape + their ASK twins q_ring_add_assoc/q_ring_add_comm/q_ring_mult_assoc now enforce them CLASS-GENERAL over every fnd:Semiring instance (reaching fnd:ringModel and fnd:fieldModel by rdfs:subClassOf), so a fnd:Ring with non-associative addition/multiplication or a fnd:Semiring with non-commutative addition goes RED; and fnd:QuasigroupDivisionShape checked only the UNIQUENESS half of Latin-square division, so fnd:QuasigroupTotalityShape + q_quasigroup_total add the EXISTENCE/TOTALITY half (every (a,b) has a left AND right division solution over the enumerated carrier), so a partial quasigroup table with a missing solution goes RED while the full-Latin-square fnd:quasigroupModel/fnd:loopModel stay GREEN. R7 ring-family axiom-completion (finding-1 HIGH + finding-2): the two-operation line reifies its two operations over fnd:hasZeroElement / fnd:hasOneElement via fnd:ringStructure (DISTINCT from the spine fnd:hasIdentityElement / fnd:opStructure the T4 fnd:MonoidIdentityShape walks), so the ADDITIVE IDENTITY (0+x=x=x+0), the MULTIPLICATIVE IDENTITY (1*x=x=x*1) and the FIELD MULTIPLICATIVE COMMUTATIVITY (a*b=b*a, the Field rung's defining upgrade, mirroring the already-present fnd:RingAddCommShape on the multiplicative op scoped to fnd:Field) were NEVER teeth-checked over the ring operations - a Semiring/Ring/Field whose declared zero fails 0+a=a, a Ring whose declared one fails 1*a=a, or a Field with a*b!=b*a passed GREEN - closed by fnd:RingAddIdentityShape (+ EXISTENCE: a fnd:Semiring with no zero -> RED), fnd:RingMultIdentityShape (+ EXISTENCE: a fnd:Ring with no one -> RED) and fnd:FieldMultCommShape + their ASK twins q_ring_add_identity / q_ring_mult_identity / q_field_mult_comm, each CLASS-GENERAL and probe-injected (real fnd:ringModel/fnd:fieldModel GREEN, each ASK FALSE on the empty graph). Additive/multiplicative CLOSURE (fnd:lawTwoOpClosure) is definitional in the reified total finite Cayley-table ring model, which does not enumerate a fnd:hasElement carrier, so additive/multiplicative closure is not a separately-bitable axiom there; the annihilator 0*x=0 is derivable (not an axiom) and is correctly NOT toothed. M1 (Magma rung parity, LOW): the base one-operation rung fnd:Magma is a CONCRETE law-bearing rung (fnd:addsLaw fnd:lawClosure) but its closure/totality law previously had NO biting tooth and NO witness model, while every sibling rung (Semigroup..AbelianGroup, Quasigroup/Loop) carried both - closed at parity by fnd:MagmaClosureShape + q_magma_closure (EXPECT-TRUE), CLASS-GENERAL over fnd:Magma, REUSING the SealedGroup closure idiom (a reified product over the op whose fnd:opResult is NOT a fnd:hasElement of the structure -> violation): for a fnd:Magma that ENUMERATES its carrier (fnd:hasElement) every reified fnd:opResult MUST be a carrier element, so a fnd:Magma with an op-result outside its enumerated carrier goes RED (probe fnd:probeMagmaOpenResult, an enumerated {A,B}-carrier magma with a fnd:opResult of fnd:elemC outside it) while the SYN worked-example witness fnd:magmaModel (a closed order-2 NON-associative magma - a bare magma, not accidentally a semigroup) and the closed Z/4 aob:witnessGroup stay GREEN; q_magma_closure is FALSE on the empty graph. W-SP0 CLASS-A/B hardening: the four witness-pinned law-teeth (fnd:SemigroupAssocShape / fnd:CommMonoidCommShape / fnd:AbelianCommShape / fnd:RingDistribShape + their ASK twins) were rewritten CLASS-GENERAL (quantifying over every rung instance by rdf:type, no hardcoded witness IRI), fnd:RingDistribShape completed to TWO-SIDED distributivity, and a new fnd:ModuleScalarLawShape + q_module_scalar_law added enforcing the FULL module scalar-action law (unitality + scalar-associativity + bi-distributivity), so a fresh violating rung instance (non-associative Semigroup, non-commutative CommutativeMonoid/AbelianGroup, non-distributive Ring, non-unital/non-distributive Module) goes RED. HONESTY LEDGER (design s0, Praeriehund, LOAD-BEARING): DS/PD/SYN over the 608 distinct fnd subjects = 52 DS + 11 PD + 545 SYN (class-level 17/1/62 of 80) + one non-fnd atom aob:witnessGroup = SYN (the sole tagged non-fnd atom, the T10 re-anchor witness). Only Monoid, the minting engine, the agnostic-progenitor pattern, Site/sheaf + 𝔗_f, and structural Set are LIFTED from Helios; every rung above Monoid, the two-operation line, quasigroup/loop, module/vector, ALL point-set spaces, the combinators/F_n/Gamma, the group inverse law, and the logic sub-floor are SYN cited standard-math fact (the Directive-19 Curry precedent) -- teeth-proved per the maximal choice, honest-red where no v1 consumer exists; the corpus's refusal of point-set topology (19/05/03) is the recorded reason those atoms are SYN not LIFTED; Curry 1936 (Tohoku Math. J. 41, 371-401) is cited, never committed. fnd:AuthorityTagShape + q_honesty_ledger make the ledger a machine-checked graph fact -- every fnd class-like/property atom carries exactly one DS/PD/SYN tag, so no SYN atom masquerades as a Helios lift. Teeth proven by PROBE INJECTION (README probe register, T1-T11 + Fix-A): each of the 45 shapes flips pyshacl conforms True->False under its probe of record; the T11 tooth caught fnd:probeUntaggedClass (no tag) and fnd:probeDoubleTag (SYN+DS masquerade), each flipping conforms and q_honesty_ledger True->False, non-vacuous on the empty graph. The ONE real re-anchor build is aob:SealedGroup rdfs:subClassOf fnd:Group (SP2's sealed group a child of the fresh agnostic fnd:Group), teeth-proved over a closed abelian Z/4 model; all other re-anchors are additive fnd:groundsIn* edges (q_reanchor_additive: no prior triple removed). Directive-18 bedrock->surface ordering is carried by hasOrdinal 0 (SP0 precedes SP1..SP9, ordinals 1..9): SP0's build/verification depends on the three committed floors staying green (its runner re-validates SP1+SP2+SP3 every run) and SP0 landed AFTER them, the build-prerequisite direction; the ONTOLOGICAL grounding (SP1/SP2/SP3 ground IN SP0) is the reverse and is carried additively by the reanchor.ttl fnd:groundsIn* edges, not by any rewrite. No phase-level silm:dependsOn edge is minted -- the SAME MD1 convention SP1/SP2/SP3 follow -- because silm:dependsOn is Workflow-typed (rdfs:domain AND rdfs:range = silm:Workflow): minting it between Phases would, under inference=rdfs, retype the phases as silm:Workflow and trip silm:WorkflowShape, breaking DAG conformance; the bedrock->surface prerequisite is therefore recorded in this prose, with the ordinal carrying the schedule. Fix-B/C/D hardening: (B, MED) the multiplicative-identity EXISTENCE clause of fnd:RingMultIdentityShape (+ q_ring_mult_identity) was scoped only to fnd:Ring, so a unit-less fnd:Semiring - itself a monoid under multiplication - passed GREEN; its EXISTENCE scope is broadened to fnd:Semiring (and thus Ring/Field), mirroring the additive fnd:RingAddIdentityShape, so a fresh unit-less fnd:Semiring goes RED while the real fnd:ringModel/fnd:fieldModel stay GREEN. (C, MED) fnd:SelfApplicationGuardShape (+ q_no_untyped_self_apply) exempted a self-application on the mere EXISTENCE of an fnd:passedGuard edge to an UNCONSTRAINED node (fnd:passedGuard fnd:propA admitted the Russell witness); the exemption now requires a GENUINE resolution - the fnd:passedGuard target must be a fnd:ContractGate/fnd:QuarantineResolution that fnd:marksProvisional the self-application while it carries silm:isProvisional true - so an ungated chi-chi behind an arbitrary passedGuard, admitted as a proposition, goes RED, and fnd:gatedSelfApplication (genuinely resolved through fnd:typedSelfAppGate, a fnd:ContractGate that marks it provisional) stays GREEN. (D, LOW) d1: the fnd:Compositor rdfs:comment cited a dangling fnd:F1 IRI, repointed to the real fnd:fnRung1 (the F_1 rung, fnd:fnDefinedAs fnd:curryFunctionality); d2: four probe-of-record identifiers named off-pattern (varStepProbe/lawKProbe/chProbe/proofProbe, a *Probe suffix the anti-drift 5c/5d self-check never greps) were renamed to the fnd:probe* prefix (fnd:probeVarStep/probeLawK/probeCh/probeProof), so the on-disk fnd:probe* union is now the true count stated here and in README (the remaining teeth use in-place perturbation). Corpus-agnostic v1 (Directive 13): zero corpus instances, built to be relaunched." .
