#     still counted it — deleting only aob:witnessLegEx aob:legTarget used to leave SHACL conforms=True AND
#     q_colimit_universal=True; cl.13 (COVERED LEG MUST FACTOR) flags any aob:coconeLeg of a testing cocone
#     lacking aob:legTarget, so FACTORING ranges over EXACTLY the covered legs and no covered leg escapes it.
#   No ASK is vacuous: every positive EXPECT-TRUE ASK returns FALSE on an empty graph (13/13 confirmed).
#   silm:isProvisional true is carried by exactly FOUR nodes in the AOB graph (verified on disk), each an
#     honest Praeriehund declaration, never a dodge: the THREE genuinely-undecidable gaps — aob:byteOrderHost
#     (host-endianness is runtime-resolved, no SP1 sibling), aob:witnessTelephone (the telephone twin's render
#     mechanism is a later sub-project, MD5), aob:contentShaAtGraduation (content_sha256-at-graduation declared
#     not computed, design s6 non-goal) — PLUS the staged-atom honesty witness aob:witnessStaged, which
#     aob:SealHonestyShape's staged branch MANDATES carry the flag (an ungraduated aob:sealState aob:staged
#     atom is not conformant-green and MUST be silm:isProvisional true; the witness inhabits that law
#     non-vacuously, so its flag is required evidence, not a dodge). SPARQL count of ?s silm:isProvisional
#     true over the 7 merged AOB data TTLs = 4 (aob:byteOrderHost, aob:contentShaAtGraduation,
#     aob:witnessStaged, aob:witnessTelephone).
#   SP2 authored NO new prim:Realization / prim:Effect (SP1's RealizationShape sh:in kept intact) and NO
#     inline anchor regex; the SP1 floor stays untouched + green (21/21 ASKs, run-floor-checks.sh).
silm:phase_w2_sp2 a owl:NamedIndividual, silm:Phase ; rdfs:label "SP2 AOB meta-ontology — colimit-taiji atom (byte descent + URN + S/O/P towers), lifted from the real base_agents WIP AOB" ; silm:hasStatus "completed" ; silm:hasOrdinal 2 .
silm:phase_w2_sp3 a owl:NamedIndividual, silm:Phase ; rdfs:label "SP3 N-dim CRS law = S/O/P towers (co-existing CRSs; coordinates derived; z grounded in the byte descent)" ; silm:hasStatus "completed" ; silm:hasOrdinal 3 ;
    rdfs:comment "COMPLETED (W2 SP3, plan T1-T13; hardened for the D1-D4 dimension-law residuals and the E1-E2 progenitor-exemption / honest-count residuals). The corpus-agnostic S/O/P-tower CRS law floor lives under basicttl/crs/ -- 5 data TTLs (carriers/towers/geometers/derivation/dual_grounding, 2233 triples), the SHACL law crs.shapes.ttl, and the ASK suite crs.queries.sparql -- and is reproducible on disk via `bash basicttl/crs/checks/run-crs-checks.sh` (exit 0, GREEN in ~24s wall). That runner proves: SP1 primitive floor green standalone (21 EXPECT-TRUE ASKs) + SP2 AOB floor green standalone (13 EXPECT-TRUE ASKs) + the single merged SP1+SP2+SP3 graph (11632 triples) conforms to crs.shapes.ttl AND to SP1 primitives.shapes.ttl re-run over the merge (prim:DualGroundingShape -- the T11 dual-grounding tooth) AND to SP2 aob.shapes.ttl, with all 10 crs + 21 SP1 + 13 SP2 EXPECT-TRUE ASKs true over the merge and the depth gate green (every crs owl:Class >=200-char rdfs:comment, 6 files). Real counts that reproduce on disk (rdflib-recounted, D4): 43 crs owl:Class, 52 crs properties (41 owl:ObjectProperty + 11 owl:DatatypeProperty), 265 minted crs individuals (each carrying a real rdfs:comment), 360 crs subjects total; 11 biting SHACL sh:NodeShape carrying 17 sh:SPARQLConstraint + 10 sh:property (sh:minCount) constraints (E1 rewrote crs:DimensionCountShape's one sh:property sh:minCount arm into two concreteness-scoped sh:sparql arms: -1 sh:property, +1 sh:SPARQLConstraint; G1 then added a third crs:DimensionCountShape sh:sparql arm -- the top-progenitor grounds-nothing DIMENSION clause -- taking the 16 to 17, and generalised crs:PlaneProgenitorShape constraint A in place from a crs:PlaneGeometer-only guard to a crs:Geometer guard with the seven-concrete-leaf enumeration, adding crs:Geometer to that shape's sh:targetClass); 10 EXPECT-TRUE ASKs; and a probe battery of 14 named crs:probe* injections on disk (the true `grep -rhoE 'crs:probe[A-Za-z0-9]+' basicttl/crs/` union -- E2 corrected the figure from 12 to 13 by adding crs:probeColourProj authored in the README probe register, and the E1 progenitor-exemption fix itself then authored the 14th identifier, crs:probeBareProg, on disk in crs.shapes.ttl + crs.queries.sparql as its bare-progenitor regression control; plus the crs:isoA/crs:isoB zero-config dimension probes of D1/D2, the crs:pA/crs:probeBareProg progenitor-exemption regression controls of E1, and the T2/T4/T12 in-place probes onto existing witnesses). Teeth are proven by PROBE INJECTION, never by absence: each of the 11 crs shapes flips pyshacl conforms True->False under its probe of record (T2 CarrierDisjointness both-carriers, T3 AxisUrnTower scalar axis, T4 NoPositionalMap S=R/O=G/P=B, T5 DimensionCount count==dim -- CONCRETENESS-SCOPED (E1) to the seven concrete geometer leaves via the exact concrete-leaf enumeration crs:PlaneProgenitorShape constraint B uses, so the zero-axis declared-dimension-5 crs:isoA mismatch (D1, OPTIONAL count -> 0 != 5) and the no-dimension crs:isoB (D2, now a concreteness-scoped dimension-present sh:sparql clause replacing the unscoped sh:property sh:minCount) stay RED as CONCRETE degeneracies, while the agnostic progenitors crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane stay GREEN when instantiated at zero axes (the crs:pA / crs:probeBareProg regression controls) -- closing the round-1 regression where the unscoped law falsely rejected a bare progenitor, T6 PlaneProgenitor symmetric family -- now including the zero-axis concrete-leaf ghost crs:probeGhostPlane closed by the same OPTIONAL count on constraint B, concreteness-scoped so the agnostic progenitors crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane stay GREEN at zero axes (D3), T7 FiveProjection joint-faithfulness, T8 FrameDerivation + DerivedNotStored, T9 ZGrounding agnostic byte-order, T10 OrderProjection S:P:O<->S:O:P, T12 NoCrossTagTransition), and T11 reuses SP1 prim:DualGroundingShape so the crs:probeOrphanChart probe flips both q_chart_dual_grounded and SP1 q_universality True->False over the merge. The two COUNT aggregates (crs:DimensionCountShape, crs:PlaneProgenitorShape constraint B) were audited (D-SWEEP) and rewritten so a degenerate ZERO-axis configuration yields count 0 (!= declared dimension / != 2) and goes RED rather than escaping an empty GROUP-BY; the ASK litmus q_dimension_equals_count / q_plane_progenitor_symmetric mirror the strengthened teeth (E1 additionally concreteness-scoped q_dimension_equals_count's two clauses via the same concrete-leaf VALUES enumeration, so a bare progenitor instance at zero axes keeps the ASK GREEN in lock-step with the shape). The E1-E2 residuals closed: crs:DimensionCountShape + q_dimension_equals_count concreteness-scoped so the agnostic progenitors crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane (which GROUND NOTHING per Q3 -- no crs:hasAxis and no crs:hasDimension triple; their rank-2 is a DECLARED FAMILY ARITY of the concrete children, not a self-grounding claim) stay GREEN at zero axes while every CONCRETE degeneracy (zero-axis, no-dimension, wrong-count) stays RED, and the geometers.ttl crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane doctrine prose made coherent with the shape; the probe figure refreshed to the true 14-identifier on-disk union (12 -> 13 by crs:probeColourProj -> 14 by crs:probeBareProg, the E1-authored bare-progenitor regression control). The G1 residual closed (the crux the E1 concreteness-scoping opened): scoping crs:DimensionCountShape's count/dimension-present arms to the seven concrete leaves EXEMPTED the TOP progenitor crs:Geometer, but crs:Geometer then had NO compensating grounds-nothing tooth (crs:PlaneProgenitorShape constraint A guarded only the crs:PlaneGeometer branch), so a node typed BARE crs:Geometer carrying a concrete crs:hasAxis / crs:hasDimension was falsely GREEN (crs:evilGeo a crs:Geometer ; crs:hasAxis crs:a,crs:b,crs:c ; crs:hasDimension 2 conformed=True; crs:evilGeo3 with one axis and crs:evilGeo4 with crs:hasDimension 7 likewise) -- contradicting crs:Geometer's own doctrine (geometers.ttl:76) and Directive 17's no-privilege symmetric coverage. G1a GENERALISED crs:PlaneProgenitorShape constraint A from a crs:PlaneGeometer-only guard to a crs:Geometer guard reusing the SAME seven-concrete-leaf enumeration (adding crs:Geometer to sh:targetClass), so a bare crs:Geometer / crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane carrying a concrete crs:hasAxis is RED symmetrically at every level. G1b ADDED crs:DimensionCountShape's third sh:sparql arm (the top-progenitor grounds-nothing DIMENSION clause): the top crs:Geometer 'declares NO concrete dimension' (geometers.ttl:76) so a bare crs:Geometer carrying crs:hasDimension is RED, while the two plane progenitors crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane stay exempt because they MAY declare their rank-2 FAMILY ARITY crs:hasDimension 2 (round-2 doctrine) -- a bare crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane at 0 axes with crs:hasDimension 2 stays GREEN. PROVEN by probe injection: crs:evilGeo (arms A+iii), crs:evilGeo3 (arm A), crs:evilGeo4 (arm iii), and a bare crs:PlaneGeometer carrying a concrete axis (arm A) each flip pyshacl conforms True->False; the GREEN regression controls (bare crs:Geometer at 0 axes + 0 dimension; bare crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane at 0 axes with crs:hasDimension 2; every concrete leaf with dim==axis-count) stay GREEN, and the round-1/2 concrete teeth (zero-axis / no-dimension concrete geometer, zero-axis concrete plane) still bite. The geometers.ttl crs:Geometer / crs:PlaneGeometer / crs:RolePairProjectionPlane prose was made coherent with the generalised teeth (top declares no dimension and is RED if it carries one; the two plane progenitors may declare family arity 2). This makes grounds-nothing enforcement SYMMETRIC across ALL progenitor levels -- no progenitor is exempted with no compensating tooth (Directive 17 no-privilege). Deps satisfied: phase_w2_sp1 and phase_w2_sp2 are completed and precede by hasOrdinal (1,2 < 3; MD1 -- no phase-level dependsOn edge, ordering carried by ordinal). The Q0-Q4 pinned rulings (Directive 17) are honoured -- agnostic progenitors throughout; z byte-order = agnostic aob:ByteOrderProgenitor with no v1 leaf (Q1); hasDimension counts tower-axes AND is per-geometer mandatory (Q2); the symmetric crs:PlaneGeometer role-pair family (Q3); chi carried only as the honest-red deferral marker crs:chiComparisonObligation, no forced Atlas<->Graph transition (Q4). Corpus-agnostic v1 (Directive 13): zero corpus instances, built to be relaunched." .
